.TH CLIPBOARD-MANAGER 1 "2026" "clipboard-manager 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clipboard-manager \- clipboard history for Linux (X11 and Wayland)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipboard-manager
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Clipboard Manager runs in the background and records text and images you
copy. Press Ctrl+Alt+C (configurable) to open the history popup and paste
any item into the window you were using.
.PP
Without a command, starts the clipboard manager in the background, or opens
the popup if it is already running.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B show
Open the history popup (starts the clipboard manager if it isn't running).
.TP
.B toggle
Open the popup, or close it if it is open. Suitable for a custom keyboard
shortcut on any desktop.
.TP
.B pause\fR, \fBresume\fR, \fBtoggle-pause
Stop or restart recording the clipboard.
.TP
.B clear
Remove all unpinned items.
.TP
.B list \fR[\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
Print the most recent items (default 20).
.TP
.B quit
Stop the running instance.
.TP
.B reload
Restart the running instance (re-reads the configuration).
.SH KEYS IN THE POPUP
.TP
.B Enter\fR, click
Paste the selected item.
.TP
.B 1 \fR\(en\fB 9\fR, \fBAlt+1 \fR\(en\fB Alt+9
Paste the first nine items directly. Plain digits paste while the search is
empty; after Ctrl+K, / or a click in the search box they are typed into the
search. Alt+digit always pastes.
.TP
.B Space
Preview the full item.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C\fR, \fBCtrl+E\fR, \fBCtrl+P\fR, \fBDelete
Copy, edit (title, text, note), pin/unpin, delete the selected item.
.TP
.B Menu\fR, \fBShift+F10\fR, right click
Open the item menu (labels, colours, preview, delete).
.TP
.B Ctrl+K\fR, \fB/
Focus the search box.
.TP
.B Home\fR, \fBEnd\fR, \fBEsc
Jump to top/bottom; clear the search or close.
.SH FILES
.TP
~/.config/clipboard-manager/config.toml
User configuration (every option is documented in the file).
.TP
~/.local/share/clipboard-manager/
History and captured images (private to the user).
.TP
~/.local/state/clipboard-manager/clipboard-manager.log
Log of the background process.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLIPBOARD_MANAGER_PROFILE=dev
Run a separate development instance with its own data and D-Bus name.
.TP
.B RUST_LOG=debug
Stay in the foreground and print a debug log.
.SH AUTHOR
Clipboard Manager contributors.
